  "worked_solution": "We write $1$ as $\\frac{3}{3}$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{3}-\\frac{4}{3}=\\frac{3-4}{3}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $3-4$ using a number line:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14148354/assets/42e6892273d3fda0560a9b0102077494944812b1e6b66e0bc96af2f0dd2c22c7.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{3-4}{3}=\\frac{-1}{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$",
